WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.560
A combination of a TV star and TV character,
viewers welcomed Richard Harrison into their

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.780
homes over several hundred episodes.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.440
His presence from the pawn shop and Pawn Stars
will be missed, and he's just as compelling

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.160
of a guy after he passed on.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.000
Richard Harrison died on June 25th, 2018,
at the age of 77.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.240
His son, Pawn Stars' Rick Harrison, confirmed
his father's passing via Instagram.

00:00:23.509 --> 00:00:27.700
Underneath a stylish shot of the Old Man,
the younger Harrison wrote, in part,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.060
"Richard Benjamin ‘The Old Man’ Harrison
passed away this morning surrounded by those

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:32.760
he loved.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.850
He will be tremendously missed by our family,
the team at Gold &amp; Silver Pawn and his many

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.000
fans the world over."

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.100
"There's a lot of memories here, and most
of those memories are with my father."

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.880
Later that day, Rick released another photo
of the Old Man this time as a young man to

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:53.170
Instagram, revealing in his caption that the
elder Harrison had, quote, "lost his long

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.040
battle with Parkinson's this morning."

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:59.900
Very few people outside of Harrison's inner
circle knew that he was sick, so his death

00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:05.440
was a surprise to most as was the cause, a
devastating, progressive neurological condition.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.060
Shortly after the Old Man died, Pawn Stars'
Austin "Chumlee" Russell" told TMZ,

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.200
"We had kind of had been preparing for it
for a while now, and I spent quite a bit of

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:18.140
time at his house this past week just knowing
that it could be coming soon and I wanted

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.760
to make sure I had plenty of time and memories
left with him while he was still here."

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.900
"This looks awesome, I'll go with you…

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.180
“No you won't, dumb-dumb, I'll go by myself."

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.200
The average viewer probably had no idea that
Harrison served in a variety of roles in the

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.800
U.S. Navy for more than 20 years.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.450
As Rick recalled in his 2011 book License
to Pawn, the Old Man stole a car when he was

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.580
17, and a North Carolina judge gave him a
choice: enlist or go to jail.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:50.360
Enlist he did, and after training, he shipped
out for tours on 2 different destroyers.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.600
Over the following years, he won promotions
all the way up to first class petty officer

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.280
and retired from the Navy in 1979.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.940
Harrison told Navy Times,

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.640
"Out of 20 years, I was deployed about 10.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.560
The only reason I got out was that I had three
teenage boys, and the wife couldn't handle

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.060
them."

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.860
Harrison died a wealthy man at the age of
77.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.540
He set up a will naming his wife and three
sons as his heirs and beneficiaries.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.380
His trusted Pawn Stars partner, Rick, was
named the executor.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.140
But according to legal papers published by
The Blast, Harrison filed an update in 2017

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.660
that he specified to make sure his son Christopher
didn't get a dime.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.590
The Old Man wrote in the document,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.380
"I would like to express my love and affection
for Christopher Keith Harrison, however, for

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.860
purposes of this Will, I have intentionally
and with full knowledge failed to provide

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.020
for him and his issue."

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.780
He gave no reason for the financial slight.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.300
So what's next for Pawn Stars?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.900
Just two days after Harrison's death, the
History Channel aired "A Treasure Remembered,"

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.440
a special tribute episode consisting of Harrison's
most memorable moments.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.540
Not long after, the show went into production
for its 16th season.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.640
Rick, Corey, and Chumlee all returned, and
no new hires were brought in to replace the

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.600
Old Man.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.980
There has been one major change for Pawn Stars,
however.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:12.240
When it returned after a long hiatus in January
2019, the show's episodes doubled in length,

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.100
expanding from a half-hour running time to
a full hour.

